From: Tariq Bashir <tbashir@brightsign.biz>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 16:07:19 +0100
Subject: Brightsign: avoid transparent flash when restoring hidden windows
 OS-20603

When opacity is set to 0, stop applying 0-opacity to the Aura content layer
and only update the platform window opacity.

Setting the Aura layer to transparent makes the GPU compositor produce a
transparent buffer. With immediate alpha commits, that stale transparent
buffer can be briefly shown when the window is made visible again.

Keep applying Aura layer opacity for non-zero values so partial transparency
continues to render correctly.

diff --git a/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_window_tree_host_platform.cc b/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_window_tree_host_platform.cc
index 744c3cce9a65c75d2b802fb61c643c82018f0ab8..94e749bdd051a97c8fcfb0fb8876dea875b93c2e 100644
--- a/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_window_tree_host_platform.cc
+++ b/ui/views/widget/desktop_aura/desktop_window_tree_host_platform.cc
@@ -757,7 +757,13 @@ bool DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::IsFullscreen() const {
 }
 
 void DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::SetOpacity(float opacity) {
-  GetContentWindow()->layer()->SetOpacity(opacity);
+  // When hiding (opacity 0), don't set the Aura compositor layer opacity.
+  // That causes the GPU compositor to render transparent buffer content,
+  // which results in a transparent frame flash when re-shown because the
+  // immediate wayland alpha commit shows the stale transparent buffer.
+  // For non-zero opacity, set both so partial transparency renders correctly.
+  if (opacity > 0.0f)
+    GetContentWindow()->layer()->SetOpacity(opacity);
   platform_window()->SetOpacity(opacity);
 }
 
